{
 "_summary": [
  "Lever A adds an in-search prefix-realizability filter (eval/realize.py:prefix_playable): before a child plan enters the frontier, its already-FIXED physical segments whose dependencies are all fixed are strict-executed with the existing two-phase+reorder machinery; children with an unplayable committed prefix are pruned. Opt-in via eval.compare --backward-prefix-check and subgoal_selfplay --prefix-check; defaults OFF, baselines unchanged (fresh plain run reproduces 120/150 exactly).",
  "No-false-pruning A/B (bench450_first150, policy_v2+value_v2, k=5, 1200 exp): every instance solved without the flag is solved with it \u2014 false prunes: 0 (plain arm), 0 (anytime arm); all 120 both-solved plain instances realize IDENTICAL move counts. Verdicts: PASS / PASS.",
  "Prefix-check alone lifts plain from 120/150 to 130/150 \u2014 the same 10 instances the anytime mode recovers, caught at push time instead of at the complete-plan pop: with the filter on, 'plan found' comes to mean 'playable plan found'.",
  "Anytime arm: 130/150 -> 130/150 (solve >= anytime-alone), mean expansions 7.3 -> 7.1 with per-instance expansions never increasing (deltas -1..-11), and one instance improves its realized moves (17 -> 16).",
  "Guidance-headroom puzzles (7 REALIZABLE_EXISTS rows of ceiling_probe_results.json) at k=5/1200: 0/7 plain, 0/7 prefix, 0/7 anytime, 0/7 anytime+prefix \u2014 none recovered. Their searches die of top-5 FRONTIER exhaustion well under budget (23-146 expansions), so the binding constraint is proposal coverage (Lever D territory), not budget wasted on doomed branches; the filter does cut the budget burned on them (636 -> 547 total anytime expansions).",
  "Self-play smoke (5 instances, random-init nets, prefix_check on): generation completes; all found winners strictly playable: True (4/4); records schema-valid: True (12 records). With the flag on, kept winners are playable by construction (the complete-pop strict check is implied).",
  "The check is one-directional by design: passing says nothing about the completion (open segments are unchecked); failing means the committed segments themselves could not be executed by the strict realizer (all robots at instance cells, no on-target condition, same two-phase+reorder retries).",
  "Only fixed segments whose full dependency closure (mover delivery chain, support placement chain, departure-after-bounce) is itself fixed are executed; anything downstream of an open edge or an unplaced stopper is skipped rather than guessed, keeping the filter permissive.",
  "Winner-ancestor probe (25 instances): every ancestor partial plan of every strictly-playable winner passes the check (0 false prunes on winning branches); on complete plans the check equals strict_moves exactly; mean cost ~0.9 ms per check (max 4.6 ms), memoized per fixed-segment multiset.",
  "Methodology unchanged: propose -> rank -> score -> best-first is untouched; the filter is pure physics (simulate.slide via eval.realize), no oracle; skeleton/astar.py, eval/end2end.py, scaling/ and move_planner*/ are not modified."
 ],
